  "summary": "Sixteen published single-cell items center on upregulated tumor and stromal programs, mainly in PDAC and glioma, mostly as candidate nominations.",
  "synthesis": "The published items cluster in pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma and glioma, where scRNA-seq and spatial transcriptomics nominate upregulated programs in malignant, stromal, and vascular compartments. Examples include SPP1-CD44 crosstalk that upregulates S100A6 in PDAC endothelial-macrophage interactions, and CTHRC1-expressing cancer-associated fibroblasts proposed as stromal biomarkers linked to poor colorectal cancer outcomes. Perturbation evidence is present but narrow: BSG loss restores enzalutamide response in prostate cancer, and macrophage pyroptosis drives luminal senescence in prostatic hyperplasia models. Most work pairs transcriptomic signatures with machine learning or prognostic cohorts. The recorded rise ratio of 2.71, with no code, industry, or seven-day star activity, describes observed activity only; no cause for the rise is inferred.",
